  "language": "en",
  "description": "This makes a total of 4 servings of Cheddar and Bacon BBQ Meatballs. Each serving comes out to be 528 calories, 34.4g fats, 1.8g net carbs, and 49.5g protein.",
  "servings": 4,
  "yield": [
    "4",
    "4 servings"
  ],
  "prepTime": "PT15M",
  "cookTime": "PT30M",
  "totalTime": "PT45M",
  "totalMinutes": 45,
  "nutrition": {
    "@type": "NutritionInformation",
    "calories": "528 kcal",
    "fatContent": "34.4 g",
    "proteinContent": "49.5 g",
    "carbohydrateContent": "1.8 g",
    "servingSize": "1 serving"
  },
  "nutritionPerServing": {
    "calories": 528,
    "netCarbsGrams": 1.8,
    "proteinGrams": 49.5,
    "fatGrams": 34.4
  },
  "ingredients": [
    "3/4 cup pork rinds",
    "24 ounce ground beef (93/7)",
    "1 large egg",
    "3/4 teaspoon salt",
    "3/4 teaspoon black pepper",
    "3/4 teaspoon cumin",
    "3/4 teaspoon garlic powder",
    "3/4 cup cheddar cheese (shredded)",
    "4 ounce bacon"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Grab your pork rinds. Mine are BBQ flavor which works perfectly for this recipe.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/Meatball_Trio-1-1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Put the pork rinds into a Ziploc bag and crush them until they are relatively fine. I don’t mind leaving a few bigger pieces in there for texture. You can also use a food processor, as shown.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/Meatball_Trio-3.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a mixing bowl, put your ground beef, egg, salt, pepper, cumin, and garlic powder.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/cheddar_and_bacon_bbq_meatballs-1-1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add your pork rind crumbs. Mix together well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/cheddar_and_bacon_bbq_meatballs-2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make a small hole in the meat and add your cheese.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/cheddar_and_bacon_bbq_meatballs-3.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix these all together well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/cheddar_and_bacon_bbq_meatballs-4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cut your bacon into thin strips. Easiest way is to use a pair of scissors. If you plan to use a knife, put your bacon in the freezer for 20 minutes prior to cutting it.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/cheddar_and_bacon_bbq_meatballs-4a.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add your bacon to a hot pan and let it fry up.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/cheddar_and_bacon_bbq_meatballs-4b.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Keep cooking your bacon until it reaches a crisp point.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/cheddar_and_bacon_bbq_meatballs-4d.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove your bacon and place on a paper towel to dry and crisp up. Keep the pan with the bacon fat in it – we will be using it to cook the meatballs!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/cheddar_and_bacon_bbq_meatballs-4e.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once your bacon has cooled off a bit, add it to the meat mixture and mix well. Roll out into meatballs and reserve beside your stove.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/cheddar_and_bacon_bbq_meatballs-5.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once all the meatballs are rolled out, add enough to a hot pan to cook without crowding each other. I don’t like cooking them all at once because they don’t turn out as well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-11",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/cheddar_and_bacon_bbq_meatballs-10.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Let them brown on one side and then flip them over.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-12",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/cheddar_and_bacon_bbq_meatballs-8.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Allow them to keep cooking, turning them on their other sides as needed. Remove them from the pan when they are rare (still semi-raw in the middle).",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-13",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/cheddar_and_bacon_bbq_meatballs-9.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook the remaining meatballs. Once they are at a rare state, add all the meatballs to the pan.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-14",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/cheddar_and_bacon_bbq_meatballs-12.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Turn down the heat to low and cover the pan with a lid. Let these cook until they are to desired wellness. I usually let them cook while I am making the BBQ sauce. By the time I’m done, they’re also done.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-15",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/cheddar_and_bacon_bbq_meatballs-11.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove the meatballs from the pan and let them rest for about 5 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-16",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/cheddar_and_bacon_bbq_meatballs-13.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve them out, usually 4-5 meatballs per person.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-17",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/cheddar_and_bacon_bbq_meatballs-17.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Apply your low-carb BBQ sauce on the top. This is to preference!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/cheddar-bacon-bbq-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-50473-step-0-18",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
